  "notes": "Exhibit A table transcribed from the rendered page image; the PDF's extracted text layer badly misaligned Make/Model/Engine/Tunes values across rows (multi-line 'Tunes' cells shifted values onto adjacent rows), so the image was used as the authoritative source. Each fitment row's part_numbers combines the leftmost 'Part Number' column value with the associated 'Tunes' column value(s) (87-89 octane and/or 91-93 octane variants), exactly as paired in that table row. One row (LPP621120, Challenger 3.6L) prints its 87-89-octane tune suffix as 'LPP621120-87-89' (with hyphen) while all other rows use the unhyphenated 'NNNN-8789' form - transcribed exactly as printed, not normalized. Execution date handwritten as '1st' confirmed from the signature page image: February 1, 2022. 'Cylinders' left null throughout since the Engine Size column states displacement only, not cylinder count; 'Induction' set to NA since no turbocharged/supercharged engine is listed."
